+# 01: Place, cancel and list holds
+
+**What to build:** A member can place a **hold** on a title when every copy is out, joining the title's **queue**. A hold is refused:
+
+- when a copy is on the shelf;
+- when the title has no copy that isn't withdrawn;
+- when the member already has an active hold on the title;
+- when the member has a copy of the title on loan.
+
+A member owing 5.00 or more (the hold **blocking threshold**, the same for every category) is **blocked** from placing holds. Holds can be cancelled. Staff can list a title's active holds in queue order. Placement order comes from sequential hold ids (`H0001`, ...). The hold blocking threshold lives in circulation policy.
+
+In this ticket no copy is ever set aside, so every hold stays `WAITING` until it's cancelled. Setting aside comes in 02.
+
+`place_hold` checks in this order: `MemberNotFound` → `AccountBlocked` → `TitleNotFound` → `HoldNotAllowed`.
+
+First step, a refactor with no change in behaviour: pull `checkout`'s inline blocking check out into one shared check, "this member's balance is at or above this threshold → `AccountBlocked`", taking the threshold as an input. `checkout` then uses it with the borrowing threshold and `place_hold` with the hold threshold; renewals will reuse it later. The existing blocking tests must pass unchanged before any hold code is written.
+
+Interface:
+- `LendingService.place_hold(member_id: str, isbn: str) -> Hold`
+- `LendingService.cancel_hold(hold_id: str) -> Hold`
+- `LendingService.holds_for(isbn: str) -> list[Hold]`
+
+Models: the `Hold` dataclass and the `HoldStatus` enum (`WAITING, READY, FULFILLED, CANCELLED, EXPIRED`), both exported from the package. New errors `HoldNotAllowed(LendingError)` (carries `reason`) and `HoldNotFound(LendingError)` (carries `hold_id`).
+
+Parent spec: `.scratch/holds/spec.md`. Vocabulary: `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] With D1 on loan to `ann`, `bob` places a hold on `dvd-1`: `WAITING`, `placed_on` today, `copy_id` and `pickup_by` both `None`
+- [ ] `HoldNotAllowed` when a copy of the title is `AVAILABLE`
+- [ ] `HoldNotAllowed` for a title with no copies, or only withdrawn ones
+- [ ] `HoldNotAllowed` for a second active hold by the same member on the same title
+- [ ] `HoldNotAllowed` when the member has a copy of the title on loan
+- [ ] `checkout` and `place_hold` share one blocking check; `checkout`'s behaviour and error contents are unchanged
+- [ ] Owing 5.00 gives `AccountBlocked` with `threshold` 5.00; owing 4.99 can place a hold; a child owing 5.00 is blocked
+- [ ] A blocked member asking about a title with a copy on the shelf gets `AccountBlocked`, not `HoldNotAllowed`
+- [ ] `MemberNotFound` and `TitleNotFound` from `place_hold`; `TitleNotFound` from `holds_for`; `HoldNotFound` from `cancel_hold`
+- [ ] `holds_for` lists active holds earliest first (`bob` then `carol`) and leaves out cancelled ones
+- [ ] `cancel_hold` on a waiting hold returns it `CANCELLED`; cancelling it again raises `HoldNotAllowed`
+- [ ] A refused hold creates nothing (`holds_for` unchanged)
+- [ ] Tests go through `LendingService` only, reusing the shared fixtures, in a new test module
+- [ ] README Concepts gains a line on holds and the hold blocking threshold (5.00)
+- [ ] Existing tests pass unchanged
