+# 04: Borrowing another copy fulfils a hold
+
+**What to build:** `add_copy` still shelves new copies as `AVAILABLE`, even when the title has a queue. So a member with an active hold on a title can end up borrowing a copy other than one set aside for them. When any `checkout` succeeds and the member has an active hold on that copy's title:
+
+- that hold becomes `FULFILLED`, and its `copy_id` records the copy actually borrowed;
+- a waiting hold fulfilled this way keeps `pickup_by` = `None`;
+- if the hold was ready on a different copy, that copy is **passed on** using the rule from 02, with no fee.
+
+Interface: `checkout(member_id, copy_id)` keeps its signature.
+
+Parent spec: `.scratch/holds/spec.md`. Vocabulary: `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (Set aside on return, and collect)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] `bob` waiting on `dvd-1`; staff `add_copy("D2", "dvd-1")`; `bob` checks out D2. His hold is `FULFILLED` with `copy_id` D2, `pickup_by` `None`, and it's gone from `holds_for`
+- [ ] `bob` ready on D1, `carol` waiting; D2 added; `bob` checks out D2. His hold is `FULFILLED` with `copy_id` D2, D1 is set aside for `carol`, and `bob`'s balance is unchanged
+- [ ] The same with nobody else waiting: D1 goes back to `AVAILABLE`
+- [ ] A refused checkout (blocked, or at the loan limit) leaves the hold as it was
+- [ ] Checkouts by members with no hold on the title behave exactly as before
+- [ ] Tests go through `LendingService` only, reusing the shared fixtures
+- [ ] Existing tests pass unchanged
