+# 02: Payments
+
+**What to build:** A member can make a **payment** of some or all of what they owe, and staff are told the new **balance**. A member can never pay more than they owe, so the balance never goes negative and there is no account credit. Payments are recorded as entries on the member's account, using the same amount checks as manual charges.
+
+Interface: `LendingService.pay(member_id: str, amount: Decimal) -> Decimal` (returns the new balance).
+
+Parent spec: `.scratch/overdue-fines/spec.md`. Vocabulary: `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Member account: manual charges and balance)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] A part payment returns and leaves the remainder (e.g. owing 5.50, paying 2.00 leaves 3.50)
+- [ ] Paying the full balance brings it to 0
+- [ ] A payment greater than the balance raises `InvalidAmount`
+- [ ] Any payment when the balance is 0 raises `InvalidAmount`
+- [ ] The same amount checks as `add_charge` apply (zero, negative, more than 2 decimal places, NaN, Infinity, `float`, `bool` all raise `InvalidAmount`; `int` accepted)
+- [ ] A rejected payment leaves the balance unchanged
+- [ ] `pay` raises `MemberNotFound` for an unknown member, checked before the amount
+- [ ] Tests go through `LendingService` only, reusing the shared fixtures
+- [ ] Existing tests pass unchanged
