+# 03: Fines on late return
+
+**What to build:** Returning a copy late charges the member a **fine** automatically, while the return itself behaves exactly as before (the loan is closed, the copy is shelved, and the same `Loan` is returned). Late days are the open days strictly after the due date, up to and including the return day: Sundays never count and there is no grace period. The fine is late days × the material's daily rate (DVD 1.00, book 0.25), and the total of fines on one loan never exceeds the title's replacement cost. Calculate it as the smaller of (late days × rate) and (replacement cost minus fines already charged on that loan), so renewals inherit the per-loan limit later. Children pay no automatic charges: this is one policy rule about member category, not a per-category rate. A fine that works out to 0 adds no entry. A fine entry records the loan, the due date it was counted from, the day it was charged and a reason such as "late return of D1".
+
+The fine calculation is a pure policy function of the due date, the day lateness is settled, the material, the replacement cost and the fines already charged on the loan. It must not read the loan's return date, so a future renewal can call it with the renewal day. Daily rates and the child exemption live in circulation policy with the other circulation numbers. Fines are charged only when lateness is settled, never accrued (ADR-0001).
+
+Interface: `LendingService.return_copy(copy_id)` keeps its signature and return value.
+
+Parent spec: `.scratch/overdue-fines/spec.md`. Vocabulary: `GLOSSARY.md`. Decision record: `docs/adr/0001-fines-charged-on-return.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Member account: manual charges and balance)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] DVD borrowed Mon 2 Mar (due Mon 9 Mar), returned Mon 16 Mar: balance 6.00 (Sunday 15 Mar not counted)
+- [ ] Book borrowed Mon 2 Mar (due Mon 23 Mar), returned Mon 30 Mar: balance 1.50
+- [ ] DVD borrowed Sat 7 Mar (due Sat 14 Mar), returned Sun 15 Mar: no fine; returned Mon 16 Mar instead: 1.00
+- [ ] A return on or before the due date charges nothing
+- [ ] DVD (replacement cost 12.00) returned 14 open days late, e.g. on Wed 25 Mar: balance 12.00, not 14.00
+- [ ] A child's late return closes the loan and shelves the copy as normal, and the child's balance stays 0
+- [ ] A fine adds to an existing balance (e.g. after a manual charge)
+- [ ] `return_copy` still returns the closed loan with `returned_on` set when a fine is charged
+- [ ] The overdue report is unchanged and its existing tests pass
+- [ ] Tests go through `LendingService` only, reusing the shared fixtures and moving the `FixedClock`
+- [ ] README Concepts gains a line on fines (rates, open days only, replacement-cost limit, children exempt)
+- [ ] Existing tests pass unchanged
