@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Lending
+
+Circulation desk for the Elm Street public library: members, the catalogue, loans, and what members owe the library.
+
+## Language
+
+### Member accounts
+
+**Account**:
+The record of what a member owes the library: every charge made against them and every payment they have made.
+_Avoid_: Ledger, wallet, tab
+
+**Charge**:
+An amount added to a member's account, increasing what they owe. Fines and no-show fees are automatic charges; manual charges are added by staff.
+_Avoid_: Fee (except in "no-show fee"), debit, debt
+
+**Fine**:
+A charge for the open days a loan ran past its due date, made when that lateness is settled.
+_Avoid_: Late fee, penalty, overdue charge
+
+**No-show fee**:
+A charge made automatically when a member does not collect a copy set aside for their hold within the pickup time.
+_Avoid_: Hold fee, uncollected charge
+
+**Manual charge**:
+A charge added to an account by staff, with a stated reason.
+_Avoid_: Adjustment, staff fee
+
+**Payment**:
+Money a member hands over to reduce what they owe.
+_Avoid_: Credit, settlement
+
+**Balance**:
+What a member owes right now: all charges on their account minus all payments.
+_Avoid_: Debt, arrears, amount due
+
+**Blocking threshold**:
+The balance at which a member may no longer perform a particular action, such as borrowing or placing a hold.
+_Avoid_: Limit (that is the number of open loans), bar
+
+**Blocked**:
+A member is blocked from an action when their balance is at or above that action's blocking threshold.
+_Avoid_: Suspended, barred, frozen
+
+### Loans
+
+**Renew**:
+To give an open loan a new due date without the copy being returned; it stays the same loan. A loan's renewals are how many times this has happened.
+_Avoid_: Extend, re-borrow, re-check-out
+
+### Holds
+
+**Hold**:
+A member's request for the next copy of a title that has no copy on the shelf.
+_Avoid_: Reservation, request
+
+**Queue**:
+The holds waiting on one title, the earliest placed first.
+_Avoid_: Line, waitlist
+
+**Set aside**:
+A returned copy is set aside when it is kept off the shelf for the hold at the front of the queue.
+_Avoid_: Reserved, held back
+
+**Ready**:
+A hold is ready once a copy has been set aside for it.
+_Avoid_: Available, waiting for pickup
+
+**Pickup time**:
+How long a ready hold waits for its member; its last day is the pickup-by date.
+_Avoid_: Grace period, hold period
+
+**Collect**:
+A member collects a hold by borrowing the copy set aside for it.
+_Avoid_: Pick up, claim
+
+**Expire**:
+A ready hold expires when its pickup time passes without the member collecting it.
+_Avoid_: Lapse, clear, time out
