 - **Title** — a catalogue entry (ISBN, material, replacement cost).
 - **Copy** — one physical item of a title, identified by its barcode.
-  `AVAILABLE` on the shelf, `ON_LOAN`, or `WITHDRAWN` for good.
+  `AVAILABLE` on the shelf, `ON_LOAN`, `ON_HOLD_SHELF` (set aside for a ready
+  hold), or `WITHDRAWN` for good.
 - **Loan** — a copy lent to a member, from `borrowed_on` to `due_on`.
   Books go out for 21 days, DVDs for 7. The library is closed on Sundays, so a
   due date that would land on a Sunday moves to the Monday.
+- **Renew** — `renew` gives an open loan a new due date without the copy
+  being returned: it stays the same loan (same loan id and `borrowed_on`),
+  due a full loan period from the renewal day, as if borrowed that day, and
+  its `renewals` count goes up by 1. The **renewal limit** is books twice,
+  DVDs never: a third renewal of a book, or any renewal of a DVD, is refused
+  with `RenewalRefused` whatever the date. A loan can be renewed from 5 days
+  before its due date onwards, with no upper bound, so an overdue loan is
+  always inside the window; earlier, `RenewalRefused` names the first day it
+  can be. A returned loan can't be renewed. Only a paid-up member can renew:
+  the renewal blocking threshold is 0.01, the same for adults and children,
+  so owing anything at all refuses it with `AccountBlocked`. That is checked
+  after the refusals paying can never fix (returned, renewal limit, too
+  early), so a member is told to pay only when paying would help. A loan
+  can't be renewed while anyone has a `WAITING` hold on its title
+  (`RenewalRefused`); a `READY` hold doesn't count, as its member already has
+  a copy set aside. Being waited for is temporary, so it is checked after the
+  balance.
+  Renewing an overdue loan charges the fine so far, worked out as if the
+  copy were returned that day (reason "late renewal of <copy>"), and then
+  moves the due date, so later lateness counts from the new due date. Fines
+  from renewals count towards the loan's replacement-cost cap, and like any
+  charge they block renewing again until paid.
+  A refused renewal changes nothing. A renewal isn't a checkout: it doesn't
+  count against the loan limit.
 - **Members** are adults (up to 8 open loans) or children (up to 4).
+- **Account** — every member's history of charges (e.g. a staff **manual
+  charge** with a reason) and payments. Their **balance** is all charges minus
+  all payments, derived from the entries and never stored; 0 for a member who
+  has never been charged. Amounts must be positive, with at most 2 decimal
+  places. A **payment** can never be more than the balance, so the balance
+  never goes below 0.
+- **Fine** — charged automatically when a copy is returned late or an
+  overdue loan is renewed, never accrued while the loan is open: DVDs 1.00
+  and books 0.25 per open day after the due date up to and including the
+  return or renewal day (Sundays never count, no grace period). All fines on one loan together never exceed the title's
+  replacement cost. Children are never fined.
+- **Blocking** — a member whose balance is at or above an action's
+  **blocking threshold** is **blocked** from it. The borrowing blocking
+  threshold is 10.00, the same for adults and children: `checkout` refuses
+  them with `AccountBlocked` until a payment brings the balance below it.
+  Nothing is stored on the member; the balance is checked at the time of each
+  blocked action (checkout, placing a hold, renewing).
+- **Hold** — a member's request for the next copy of a title with no copy on
+  the shelf, joining that title's **queue** (earliest placed first, by hold id
+  `H0001`, ...). Refused while a copy is on the shelf, when every copy is
+  withdrawn, when the member already has an active hold on the title, or when
+  they have a copy of it on loan. The hold blocking threshold is 5.00, the same
+  for adults and children. A hold is `WAITING` until a copy comes back or it is cancelled.
+- **Set aside** — a returned copy whose title has waiting holds goes
+  `ON_HOLD_SHELF` for the first of them, which becomes `READY`. The **pickup
+  time** is 7 days: the pickup-by date is 7 calendar days after the copy was
+  set aside, moved to the Monday if that is a Sunday. With nobody waiting the
+  copy goes back on the shelf. A set-aside copy is not available to anyone
+  else and can't be withdrawn.
+- **Collect** — the member borrows the set-aside copy with an ordinary
+  `checkout` (still subject to blocking and the loan limit), and the hold is
+  `FULFILLED`. Borrowing any other copy of the title (say, a new copy, which
+  `add_copy` always shelves) fulfils the hold too, recording the copy
+  borrowed; a copy set aside for it is passed on, at no charge. Cancelling a
+  hold is free; cancelling a ready one passes its copy on to the next waiting
+  hold, with a fresh pickup-by date, or back to the shelf.
+- **Expire** — the daily job `expire_holds` expires every `READY` hold whose
+  pickup-by date has passed, charges the member a 1.00 **no-show fee**
+  (children are never charged), and passes the copy on as a cancellation
+  would. It returns the holds it expired, catches up after skipped days, and
+  expires nothing on a second run the same day. Until the job runs, a ready
+  hold can still be collected. Waiting holds never expire. No-show fees count
+  towards every blocking threshold.
 
 ## Conventions
 
